# LaTeX build products. The paper now lives in paper/ and is authored in LaTeX directly, so
# the .tex files there are source and are tracked, as are the generated_*.tex files it \inputs.
# The PDF and .bbl are tracked deliberately: they are the submission deliverables. Everything
# below is pure latexmk churn that would produce a diff on every rebuild.
paper/**/*.aux
paper/**/*.blg
paper/**/*.fls
paper/**/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/**/*.log
paper/**/*.out
paper/**/*.toc
paper/**/*.synctex.gz
paper/**/missfont.log

# Per-figure proof sheets. Each figures/*/ carries a preview.tex that builds the figure
# standalone so it can be looked at without recompiling the manuscript. The preview.tex is
# source and is tracked; the PDF it builds and the rasterisations taken off that PDF are
# churn on every redraw, like the .aux and .log above.
paper/**/figures/**/preview.pdf
paper/**/figures/**/prev-*.png
paper/**/figures/**/big-*.png

# Agent worktrees. Each is a full checkout of this repository living inside it, so an
# unqualified `git add -A` would otherwise stage a copy of the tree into itself.
.claude/worktrees/

# Local scratch, not part of the project record.
.codex/
output/

# built Overleaf bundle, regenerate with scripts/build_overleaf_bundle.sh
paper/*_overleaf.zip

